oppen Commercial Source License
Version 1.0, 2026-09-04

Copyright 2026 oppen contributors

This licence governs `apps/desktop` — the Tauri shell and the Vue operator
console, together with the quant layer and the workflow engine that ship inside
them. It does not govern `crates/`, which is the open core and is licensed under
Apache-2.0; see the LICENSE file at the root of this repository. Which code sits
on which side of that line, and why the line is where it is, is recorded as
decisions L1 and L2 in docs/decisions.md.

The source in this directory is published so that it can be read. It is not
open source, and the difference is deliberate: the safety claims oppen makes are
claims about the core, the core is Apache-2.0 so that those claims can be
checked, and nothing above the core carries a claim that requires the right to
redistribute in order to verify.

1. DEFINITIONS

   "The Software" means the contents of this directory and any derivative work
   of it. "You" means the individual or entity exercising the permissions below.
   "Official Build" means a binary distributed by the oppen maintainers.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a. Read, copy and retain the source, for any purpose.

   b. Build the Software and run your own builds.

   c. Use the Software to trade, including for profit, on your own account or on
      the account of an entity you control or are employed by. Trading with
      oppen is what it is for; nothing in this licence restricts what you trade,
      how much, or on whose behalf, and no separate commercial licence is
      required to trade with your own build.

   d. Modify the Software for your own use under 2(b) and 2(c), and submit those
      modifications to the Project under the CLA.

   e. Publish excerpts and analysis, including security research and adversarial
      findings, without prior permission and without notice to the maintainers.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   a. Distribute the Software, modified or unmodified, in source or binary form,
      to any third party.

   b. Offer the Software to third parties as a hosted or managed service.

   c. Sublicense, sell, rent or lease the Software.

   d. Remove, disable or alter the builder code configured in an Official Build,
      in any copy you distribute. This restriction does not apply to a build you
      run yourself under 2(b) and 2(c). The fee is disclosed in README.md and is
      bounded by a maximum rate you sign; decisions M1, M2 and L5 record the
      rates and the reasoning.

   e. Use the "oppen" name or mark to identify any build that is not an Official
      Build. See NOTICE.

4. RESERVED RIGHTS

   All rights not expressly granted in section 2 are reserved. No patent licence
   is granted by this licence. The maintainers may offer the Software to any
   party under different terms, including terms permitting the activities in
   section 3, by separate written agreement.

5. NO WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
   OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
   SOFTWARE.

   Trading carries risk of total loss. The safety properties oppen documents are
   described in docs/threat-model.md, which states what they do and do not
   defend against. Read it before trading real funds.

6. TERMINATION

   Your permissions under section 2 end automatically if you breach section 3
   and do not cure the breach within 30 days of becoming aware of it. Permissions
   granted to anyone who received the Software from the maintainers directly are
   not affected by your breach.

